{"id": "EUVD-2026-86988", "enisaUuid": "e4fc6c72-8075-398a-8a2a-584d56463ee9", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nEDAC/device_sysfs: Use kstrtouint() for poll_msec to prevent truncation\n\nThe poll_msec sysfs store file uses simple_strtoul() which accepts an unsigned\nlong, but the target field (poll_msec) is unsigned int. On 64-bit systems,\na value > UINT_MAX is silently truncated when stored.\n\nFix the mismatch by using kstrtouint() instead. This rejects values larger\nthan UINT_MAX at parse time, making truncation impossible. Also add a check\nfor value < 1 to reject the 0-delay case, which would cause the poll work to\nspin without delay and consume 100% CPU.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:27", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:51", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a60794ee3f453516ab3ed212ba0295ecf890bc8c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f856511058c8cb470d6c6c7ce908870adcdc7dc6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/656e2fe98ac452db4e5b8147d1f33b8c35b4ec4b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/541fc6f733b32463cf23277637bb07e2aaa00b53", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ea01c061d839b520f385f112908de1c6e3391327", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/528052af901d6e6bbfa0e52362a70a58a5dd1e43", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0e022ee4f8e0dc843ba4c80bb75408a7704279af", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/66cc9dec919dd63d8e4b3d386f7aed3ae684e645"], "aliases": ["GHSA-r5h3-8gfg-g75q", "CVE-2026-98157"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06498197-f202-3dc6-aa90-87bca9c15ab1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e27e3dac651771fe3250f6305dee277bce29fc5d <f856511058c8cb470d6c6c7ce908870adcdc7dc6"}, {"id": "39c539e2-049d-3979-bd14-fd0aca4ab176", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "3ec0e42e-1042-3906-ace5-c6c1233611f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"na